NUM-06: use the HDS-5 slope correction +0.7*S for mitered culvert inlets, not +7*S

culvert_getInflow() stores the slope correction with the opposite sign to
HDS-5 (HW/D = ... - scf), so scf = 0.5*S reproduces HDS-5's -0.5*S for most
inlets. For mitered inlets (codes 5, 37, 46) HDS-5 and the SWMM Hydraulics
Reference Manual (eq. 7-39/7-46) use +0.7*S, i.e. scf = -0.7*S, but the code
has -7.0*S. Mitered culverts therefore get ten times the correction: at a 5%
slope their inlet-control headwater is 0.32*D too high. Use -0.7.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-06_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/culvert.c b/src/legacy/engine/culvert.c
index 5f62877..c036ee6 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/culvert.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/culvert.c
@@ -201,12 +201,12 @@ double culvert_getInflow(int j, double q0, double h)
     culvert.yFull = culvert.xsect->yFull;
     culvert.ad = culvert.xsect->aFull * sqrt(culvert.yFull);
 
-    // --- slope correction factor (-7 for mitered inlets, 0.5 for others)
+    // --- slope correction factor (-0.7 for mitered inlets, 0.5 for others)
     switch (code)
     {
     case 5:
     case 37:
-    case 46: culvert.scf = -7.0 * Conduit[k].slope; break;
+    case 46: culvert.scf = -0.7 * Conduit[k].slope; break;
     default: culvert.scf = 0.5 * Conduit[k].slope;
     }
 
